## TCF — ternary missing-colour completion

For every integer $n\ge1$, the finite carrier is
$X_n=\{0,1,2\}^{\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z}$. All coordinates update from the
same original snapshot. If $a=x_i$ and $b=x_{i+1}$, put

$$T(x)_i=\begin{cases}
a+1\pmod3,&a=b,\\
\text{the unique element of }\{0,1,2\}\setminus\{a,b\},&a\ne b.
\end{cases}$$

This declaration is not a proposed admission. Internal comparison searches
and direct public-primary retrieval/read precede this proof dossier.
Preliminary algebraic subtraction was used only to choose the nearest
primary comparator; no numerical exploration occurred.

Disposition: `KILL_VALUE_TEMPORAL_CAPTIVE_BALLISTIC_WRAPPER / NO_PROMOTION`.
The full reduction is in `PROOF_AND_DISPOSITION.md`. Once the temporal
subtraction closed, no independent inverse/extremum proof project was
started merely to compensate for it.

